Z||000000||Enterra||12-05-2001||06:29 PM||||Tried calling you today, you are a very busy man.<P>I have a manual trans kit, but I decided to go 4 speed auto instead.<BR> <BR>just wanted to ask if a manual trans kit will fit onto an auto car. Are all the mounting brackets on the engine the same or are they different. Also, which flexplate would you recommend using. I have a few 152 teeth sitting here now as well as an AOD from a caddy.<P>Any tips would be helpful. TIA ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Archie||12-05-2001||11:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Enterra:<BR><B>Tried calling you today, you are a very busy man.<P>I have a manual trans kit, but I decided to go 4 speed auto instead.<BR> <BR>just wanted to ask if a manual trans kit will fit onto an auto car. Are all the mounting brackets on the engine the same or are they different. Also, which flexplate would you recommend using. I have a few 152 teeth sitting here now as well as an AOD from a caddy.<P>Any tips would be helpful. TIA </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Our Stick shift kits use an adapter plate and Flywheel that is specifically designed for and works with stick shift cars only. Our automatic kits use an adapter plate and a Flex Plate adapter that are specifically designed for and work with Automatic cars only. In other wordsout stick and automatic kits are not interchangeable.<P>On automatics, in all cases, we use the Flexplate from the 4 cylinder Fiero.<P>Hope this helps<P>Archie<P>------------------<BR>Just how fast do you want to go?||||reg||1
